    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0698" n="688" xml:id="pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P.W./304</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hu
                        Shih</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="40" xml:id="d722-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-29">July 29, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have just received a
                    telegraphic message from Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek which he desires to be
                    conveyed to the President. I shall be grateful if you will be so good as to
                    transmit it to its high destination.</p>
                <p>I wish to take this opportunity to express to you the deep gratification felt by
                    my Government and people over the statement which you made on July 24th in
                    regard to Japanese aggression in Indo-China<anchor n="41" xml:id="d722-f2"/> and
                    over the measures which the United States Government has taken for the freezing
                    control of Chinese and Japanese assets.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hu Shih</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d722-a1.xml" xpointer="d722-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d722-f1" n="40" type="source" xml:id="d722-f1-content">
                <p>The Acting Secretary transmitted the Chinese Ambassador’s note with enclosure to
                    President Roosevelt on July 30 and acknowledged them on July 31.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d722-f2" n="41" xml:id="d722-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1931-41v02#pg_315">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 315</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
